# [DINRG](../wg/dinrg.html)

## Summary

The Decentralized Internet Infrastructure Research Group (DINRG) met to discuss ongoing research into Internet consolidation, centralization, and architectural countermeasures. The session featured presentations on Encrypted Client Hello (ECH) deployment and its privacy vs. consolidation tradeoffs, platform dependencies and centralization risks in Passkeys, practical architecture for decentralized end-to-end collaborative applications, security vulnerabilities in early attestation protocols for confidential computing, and a general discussion on tracking global cloud outage incidents as indicators of infrastructure centralization.

