### 5. Architecting Decentralized End-to-End Applications: Reinstalling End-to-End Principles
- **Presenter:** Tianyuan Yu
- **Slides:** [Architecting Decentralized End-to-End Applications: Reinstalling End-to-End Principles](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-dinrg-architecting-decentralized-end-to-end-applications-reinstalling-end-to-end-principles-00)
- **Technical Content:**
  - Introduced **ONLY** ("ON the THING"), a decentralized, in-browser collaborative document editor designed to eliminate reliance on central cloud providers (e.g., Google Docs).
  - Uses DNS names and email addresses for user identity, browser local storage for document persistence, Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs) for consistency, and Message Layer Security (MLS) for group key management and encryption.
  - Relies on Named Data Networking (NDN) testbed nodes as a semantic overlay network for packet forwarding by content and schema names rather than IP addresses.
  - Demonstrated the bootstrapping flow: domain controllers act as local trust anchors, issuing certificates and security schemas over NDN without centralized authorization servers.

