### 6. EarlyAttestationBleed and EarlyAttestationTschüss
- **Presenter:** Muhammad Usama Sardar
- **Slides:** [EarlyAttestationBleed and EarlyAttestationTschüss](https://datatrestationbleed-and-earlyattestationtschuss-00)
- **Technical Content:**
  - Formal analysis of early attestation protocols used in confidential computing environments (such as Attested TLS deployments for European electronic health record systems).
  - Contrasted early intra-handshake attestation with standard post-handshake attestation using RFC 9261 (Exported Authenticators for TLS).
  - Identified critical architectural vulnerabilities resulting in 39 GitHub security advisories and 20+ CVEs (including CVSS scores up to 9.6). Main root causes: missing TLS connection binding (enabling relay attacks) and missing hardware binding (enabling host diversion attacks).
  - Disclosed vulnerabilities to maintainers; open-source projects and vendor stacks (RustLS implementations, Go libraries, Cocos AI, Confidential Computing Consortium references) have archived or retired early attestation in favor of standard post-handshake attestation.
  - Raised open research questions regarding how to decentralize confidential computing workloads (e.g., via federated learning) to avoid single-cloud provider lock-in.

