### 7. Tracking Outages as Centralization Indicators
- **Discussion Lead:** Andrew Campling
- **Technical Content:**
  - Suggested that DINRG track and catalog large-scale cloud infrastructure outages (such as recent global Microsoft service disruptions) over time to measure the real-world operational impacts of Internet centralization.
  - **Lixia Zhang, Dirk Kutscher, & Matthias Wählisch:** Noted previous analytical work (e.g., paper/draft "The Internet runs on names") showing how the Internet shifted from IP-level path resilience to name-based application steering, increasing complexity and single-point-of-failure risks. Agreed that systematically documenting such incidents is valuable work for the group.

